Third-party sound chip cores used by pkg/audio/vgm
==================================================

Only chip emulation cores are vendored. The VGM interpreter, DAC stream
engine, data block handling, resampler, mixer, per-chip glue (engine.c,
chip_*.c) and every header under ../csrc are Zaparoo code under
GPL-3.0-or-later. The ../csrc headers declare the types, macros and
functions the cores use; they are written from the cores' own definitions and
contain no libvgm framework, glue or player code.

Upstreams
---------

libvgm   https://github.com/ValleyBell/libvgm
         commit c5c03a2c2514d38d2ab7b7e8dbd021af0b8292cb (2026-11-04)
         files from emu/cores/, copied into libvgm/cores/
emu2413  https://github.com/digital-sound-antiques/emu2413
         commit a1d5120903b75f93d3eb7690e34a29c0b4add903 (2026-10-11), v1.6.4
         emu2413.c, emu2413.h and LICENSE, copied into emu2413/

