License texts
-------------

BSD-3-Clause   LICENSE.BSD-3-Clause.txt (copyright holders are named in each file)
GPL-2.0        LICENSE.GPL-2.0.txt (the files allow version 2 or any later version)
LGPL-2.1       LICENSE.LGPL-2.1.txt (the files allow version 2.1 or any later version)
MIT            LICENSE.MIT-mikey.txt for mikey.c, emu2413/LICENSE for emu2413

Changes and replacements
------------------------

- libvgm/cores/fmopn.c: two changes, marked "Zaparoo". The YM2610 ADPCM-A
  fetch checks the address against the ROM size, because the end address
  comes from the file. The legacy-mode 3CH FNUM1 latch read only runs for
  the first port, where the channel index fits block_fnum[3].
- libvgm/cores/segapcm.c: SEGAPCM_update, marked "Zaparoo", reads
  silence past the ROM.
- libvgm/cores/upd7759.c: ROM reads go through zap_rom_byte, marked
  "Zaparoo", which checks the bank offset plus address against the ROM size,
  because the bank, sample index and offsets come from the file.
- libvgm/cores/multipcm.c: init_sample and read_byte, marked "Zaparoo",
  check the ROM exists and the read stays inside it. value_to_fixed
  saturates instead of overflowing the float cast, because the pitch table
  scales with the chip clock from the file.
- libvgm/cores/k054539.c: k054539_w and k054539_r, marked "Zaparoo", drop
  register offsets past the 0x230-byte register file, because the offset
  comes from the file.
- libvgm/cores/x1_010.c: seta_sound_w, seta_sound_r and seta_update,
  marked "Zaparoo", keep register offsets, waveform and envelope numbers
  inside the 0x2000-byte register area and PCM reads inside the ROM.
- libvgm/cores/es5503.c: es5503_halt_osc, marked "Zaparoo", skips the
  sync partner below oscillator 0.
- libvgm/cores/iremga20.c: irem_ga20_cache_samples, marked "Zaparoo",
  stops the voice when the ROM is missing or the address is past it.
- libvgm/cores/k051649.c: the waveform, volume and frequency handlers,
  marked "Zaparoo", ignore channel numbers past the fifth.
- libvgm/cores/scsp.c: SCSP_UpdateSlot, marked "Zaparoo", wraps sample
  addresses to the sample RAM.
- libvgm/cores/scspdsp.c: SCSPDSP_Step, marked "Zaparoo", checks DSP memory
  addresses against the RAM's real word count.
- ../csrc/emu/cores/ymdeltat.c and .h: our own ADPCM-B (DELTA-T) decoder for
  Y8950, YM2608 and YM2610, used in place of libvgm's ymdeltat.c, whose
  header grants no license.
- ../csrc/emu/cores/fmopn_2608rom.h: an all-zero stand-in. The real file is a
  dump of Yamaha's YM2608 rhythm ROM, with no license that allows
  redistribution. The glue drops rhythm writes, so the YM2608 rhythm part
  plays silent.
- ../csrc/emu/cores/scspdsp.h: our own declaration of the SCSP DSP state;
  libvgm's copy has no license header.

Every other vendored file is byte-for-byte identical to upstream.

Not included
------------

YMF278B (OPL4), WonderSwan, NES FDS and ES5506 are not emulated: their
commands are parsed and skipped, and those parts play silent.
